# Kestrel update trust anchor -- ssh-keygen allowed_signers format.
#
# This file lists the public key(s) that may sign in-place (app-layer) update
# manifests. While it contains no key line (only blanks and these comments),
# release signing is OFF and updates install exactly as before -- unsigned.
#
# To REQUIRE signed updates, add one line per trusted signer, in the
# ssh-keygen allowed_signers format:
#
#     <principal> <keytype> <base64-public-key>
#
# e.g.  kestrel-release ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...
#
# The matching PRIVATE key is held only as the Release workflow's
# UPDATE_SIGNING_KEY secret and is NEVER committed. Once a key line is present,
# every offered release must ship a valid update-manifest.json.sig over this
# key or the device refuses it (a refusal that --force cannot override).
#
# The trust anchor is pinned at flash time: the in-place update engine does not
# rewrite this file, so changing or rotating the trusted key is a reflash. See
# docs/developer/updates-setup.md ("Signing releases").
